            <ArticleTitle>[Role of substance P and calcitonin gene-related peptide in bone metabolism].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>334-339</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11817/j.issn.1672-7347.2017.03.016</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Substance P (SP) and calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP) are the neuropeptides released from the sensory nerve endings. Neuropeptides play a role in bone and the relevant organs. It exerts functions in regulation of the bone metabolism, fracture healing and pain by a certain way. The biological properties and distributions of SP and CGRP are closely related to the pathogenesis and development of bone metabolism, fracture healing and pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
